      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In today's hyper-transparent digital environment, neutrality often functions as a liability rather than a strategy because it fuels the narrative that your brand is indifferent to critical issues. A long-term business case for silence only holds if you can confidently articulate that your core product and operational ethics are independent of the bill itself, but even then, public perception frequently overrides technical arguments. Ultimately, attempting to remain neutral on such a divisive issue without providing a clear alternative stance is likely a losing battle that will erode trust across all demographics.",
